From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stanley Jhu <stanleyjhu@google.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:08:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 15/27] scsi: ufs: bsg: Abort ufs_bsg_request() when runtime
 resume fails

ufs_bsg_request() resumes the UFS device W-LUN with ufshcd_rpm_get_sync()
and ignores its return value:

 1. The W-LUN is runtime suspended.
 2. User space submits a BSG request.
 3. ufs_bsg_request() calls ufshcd_rpm_get_sync().
 4. The W-LUN runtime resume fails and the W-LUN stays suspended.
 5. ufshcd_rpm_get_sync() returns a negative errno, which is ignored.
 6. ufs_bsg_request() dispatches the BSG command while the W-LUN is
    still suspended.

Use ufshcd_rpm_resume_and_get() and jump to out_complete on error so the
BSG job is completed via bsg_job_done() with the failure code without
dropping an unacquired runtime PM reference.

Fixes: b294ff3e3449 ("scsi: ufs: core: Enable power management for wlun")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org # needs "scsi: ufs: core: Introduce ufshcd_rpm_resume_and_get() helper"
Signed-off-by: Stanley Jhu <stanleyjhu@google.com>
Reviewed-by: Bart Van Assche <bvanassche@acm.org>
Reviewed-by: Peter Wang <peter.wang@mediatek.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261029040003.2100003-5-stanleyjhu@google.com
Signed-off-by: Martin K. Petersen (Oracle) <mkp@kernel.org>
(cherry picked from commit 2b8541edf7c43f0294c45d2e687bbc1288292f4e)
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/ufs/core/ufs_bsg.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/core/ufs_bsg.c b/drivers/ufs/core/ufs_bsg.c
index baf6ae917..8df1a2c6a 100644
--- a/drivers/ufs/core/ufs_bsg.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/core/ufs_bsg.c
@@ -150,7 +150,9 @@ static int ufs_bsg_request(struct bsg_job *job)
 		goto out_complete;
 	}
 
-	ufshcd_rpm_get_sync(hba);
+	ret = ufshcd_rpm_resume_and_get(hba);
+	if (ret)
+		goto out_complete;
 
 	msgcode = bsg_request->msgcode;
 	switch (msgcode) {
-- 
